sequenceDiagram
    actor Owner
    participant GuiController as RequestsController.cs<br/>(GUI-BRAP)
    participant Proxy as RequestProxyServiceAdapter.cs
    participant ApiClient as RequestService.cs<br/>(ApiClient)
    participant ApiController as RequestsController.cs<br/>(Api)
    participant Service as RequestService.cs<br/>(Api)
    participant RequestRepo as RequestRepository.cs
    participant NotificationService as NotificationService.cs
    participant NotificationRepo as NotificationRepository.cs
    participant DB as AppDbContext

    Note over Owner,GuiController: Offer approves the request and creates the rental.

    Owner->>GuiController: Offer(int id)
    GuiController->>GuiController: Guid ownerAccountId = User.GetAccountId()
    GuiController->>Proxy: OfferGameAsync(id, new RequestActionDataTransferObject { AccountId = ownerAccountId })
    Proxy->>ApiClient: OfferGameAsync(requestId, body)
    ApiClient->>ApiController: HTTP PUT /api/requests/{requestId}/offer
    ApiController->>Service: OfferGame(requestId, body.AccountId)
    Service->>RequestRepo: Get(requestId)
    RequestRepo->>DB: RequestsWithNavigations(...).FirstOrDefault(...)
    DB-->>RequestRepo: request / null
    RequestRepo-->>Service: req / throw KeyNotFoundException

    alt request not found
        Service-->>ApiController: Failure(OfferError.NotFound)
    else owner is not request owner
        Service-->>ApiController: Failure(OfferError.NotOwner)
    else request is not open
        Service-->>ApiController: Failure(OfferError.RequestNotOpen)
    else request is open
        Service->>Service: buffStart / buffEnd
        Service->>RequestRepo: GetOverlappingRequests(req.Game?.Id ?? MissingForeignKeyId, req.Id, buffStart, buffEnd)
        RequestRepo->>DB: RequestsWithNavigations(...).Where(...)
        DB-->>RequestRepo: overlapping requests
        RequestRepo-->>Service: conflicts

        Service->>RequestRepo: ApproveAtomically(req, conflicts)
        alt approval transaction succeeds
            RequestRepo->>DB: ExecuteDelete + Rentals.Add(newRental) + SaveChanges + Commit
            DB-->>RequestRepo: rentalId
            RequestRepo-->>Service: rentalId

            loop for conflicting requests
                Service->>NotificationService: SendNotificationToUser(conflict.RenterId, BookingUnavailable)
                NotificationService->>NotificationRepo: Add(notification)
                NotificationRepo->>DB: Notifications.Add(...) + SaveChanges()
            end

            Service->>NotificationService: SendNotificationToUser(renterId, RentalRequestApproved)
            NotificationService->>NotificationRepo: Add(notification)
            NotificationRepo->>DB: Notifications.Add(...) + SaveChanges()

            Service-->>ApiController: Success(rentalId)
        else transaction fails
            RequestRepo-->>Service: throw Exception
            Service-->>ApiController: Failure(OfferError.TransactionFailed)
        end
    end

    ApiController-->>ApiClient: HTTP response
    ApiClient-->>Proxy: ServiceResult<int>.Ok(rentalId) / failed result
    Proxy-->>GuiController: success / exception
    GuiController-->>Owner: Redirect to Others with message
